WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.100
- [Narrator] This satellite
image shows a field

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.160
outside the eastern
Ukrainian town of Vuhledar,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.400
littered with destroyed
tanks and infantry vehicles.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.670
Ukrainian and Western officials
say this is the results

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.070
of a battle which has already cost Russia

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.100
dozens of military vehicles
and hundreds of troops

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.273
since February.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.960
The coal mining town in
Ukraine became a new focus

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.260
of Russia's offensive due
to a strategic location.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.320
From here, Ukrainian forces
can target rail lines

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.070
linking Russian-occupied Donetsk
to the Crimean Peninsula,

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.800
a major base for Moscow's operations.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.020
The Wall Street Journal
analyzed videos taken

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.820
within two miles of Vuhledar,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.670
and we spoke to British and
American military experts

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.640
to find out what this offensive
reveals about the state

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.103
of Russia's army a year into the war.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.720
In late February, Ukraine's
Army shared this video

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.243
of an intersection just outside Vuhledar.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.750
Kyiv says it shows a
Russian armored vehicle

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.433
running over a landmine.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.510
The area, where at least
seven other vehicles appear

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.780
to have been damaged, looks
like what military experts call

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.370
a choke point.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.100
As the video shows,
Russian troops strove down

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.260
a narrow route to the intersection,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.520
making them easy targets for
mines and Ukrainian fire.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.470
Despite the obvious dangers,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.043
Russian tanks seem to roll
onto the same trap again,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.310
and again, as we see in another
video released a week later.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.380
Ukrainian soldiers on the front lines say

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.093
Russian forces kept making similar moves.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:38.426
(soldier speaking foreign language)

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.090
- [Narrator] Military experts
who watched these videos

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.910
say this shows that Russian
troops received orders

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:03.060
from the top, and most likely
didn't have the autonomy

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.610
to adjust to the situation on the ground.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.150
And that is an extreme example
of how Russia's military

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.360
didn't adapt from the old
command and control system

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.130
from the Soviet's era.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.320
Another issue the analyst pointed out

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.930
is that it appears the area
wasn't cleared of mines

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.940
before the tanks moved forward.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.940
Soldiers would normally use
smoke to cover themselves

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:28.110
from enemy shells, but videos
show it didn't happen here.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:31.380
Military analysts say one reason
could be the poor training

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.873
of recently-mobilized Russian soldiers.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.010
Russia's army has paid a high price

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.600
for the decisions in Vuhledar.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.240
Ukraine said it destroyed
at least 30 tanks

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.170
and infantry-fighting vehicles
within 10 days in February.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.300
(weapon firing)

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.790
- The whole Russian brigade
was effectively annihilated

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:51.840
or destroyed.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.170
They lost nearly 1,000, or
over 1,000 people in two days.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.390
- [Narrator] Russia's Defense
Ministry didn't respond

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.180
to the Journal's questions
on the losses in Vuhledar,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.000
but its spokespeople have
repeatedly claimed successes

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.038
against Kyiv's forces in
parts of southeastern Ukraine.

00:03:07.038 --> 00:03:11.371
(soldier speaking foreign language)

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.070
(weapon firing)

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.460
Some experts believe Russia's
hasty offensive in Vuhledar

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.430
could be due to the Kremlin's
desire to show results

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.520
after months without major victories.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.430
Western officials say the
Russian army has been plagued

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.150
by chronic issues such as an
ineffective command structure,

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.820
and poor training since
the start of the war.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.190
And the setbacks in
Vuhledar suggest the issues

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.380
haven't been resolved on the battlefield.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.260
One military expert said
Vuhledar shows a high price

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.060
the Kremlin is willing to pay.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.610
Russia hopes to overcome
Ukraine's resistance

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.130
with more soldiers and military hardware

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.493
before Western weapons arrive
to help the Ukrainians.

